course: dictionary
lesson: 15135
title: A cheeky word: scallywag
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell you how a person feels as well as what they did. Read the words around the word, and look for clues. «"You little scallywag!" laughed Grandma, as Sam ate the last biscuit.» Grandma is laughing, so she is not really cross. A scallywag is someone who is naughty in a cheeky, lovable way.
explain: Look at the example «The scallywags crept onto the ship at midnight, hoping to steal the gold.» Here the word means naughty rascals who are up to mischief. The story is not kind to them, so the feeling is not playful, but the word still means rascals.
explain: Ask yourself: would the word fit if I swapped in "rascal"? Scallywag and rascal are close in meaning, so the swap should still make sense. If it does, you have found the meaning.
fact: «Scallywag» means a child or person who behaves badly in a cheeky, likeable way: a rascal.
fact: It is informal and old-fashioned, so people often say it with a smile, as in «you little scallywag».
fact: Common phrases are «you little scallywag» and «a bunch of scallywags».
fact: In US history, «scalawag» (spelt with an a) was an insult for white Southerners who supported the Union government after the American Civil War.
exercise: «"You little scallywag!" laughed Grandma, as Sam ate the last biscuit.» What does scallywag mean here? | A very tired old horse | A kind nurse who looks after sick children | A clever scientist who wins prizes | *A cheeky child who is naughty in a likeable way
exercise: «The scallywags crept onto the ship at midnight, hoping to steal the gold.» What were the scallywags doing? | *Sneaking onto a ship to steal | Singing a happy song | Sleeping in a warm bed | Cooking a big feast
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as scallywag? | blanket | *rascal | whisper | mountain
test: «"Put that down, you scallywag," said Dad, but he was smiling.» Why is Dad smiling? | He is angry and wants to shout | He is fast asleep | He has never seen a child before | *He is cross, but he still loves the cheeky child
test: The word scallywag is informal. What does informal mean? | *Relaxed, the sort of word used in everyday chat | Very serious and used only in court | Made of metal | Written in a foreign language
exam: Which describes a scallywag best? | A tall tree in the park | A very polite head teacher | A type of cold soup | *A cheeky, likeable rascal who causes mischief
